//Approach

Assume the first string is the longest common prefix.

Traverse the remaining strings one by one.

Check whether each string starts with the current prefix using startsWith().

If it does not, remove the last character of the prefix using substring().

Repeat until a common prefix is found or the prefix becomes empty.

Return the final prefix.//









class Solution {
    public String longestCommonPrefix(String[] strs) {
        String prefix = strs[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < strs.length; i++) {
            while (!strs[i].startsWith(prefix)) {
                prefix = prefix.substring(0, prefix.length() - 1);

                if (prefix.isEmpty()) {
                    return "";
                }
            }
        }

        return prefix;
    }
}
